Oliver Scholz wrote:
> I'd appreciate some advice on early-game pacifism and on the
> particular problem stated below.
>
> One problem I am facing is that it seems nearly impossible to survive
> the Gnomish Mines in this style. The large space and especially the
> darkness make it a hazard without proper equipment (and I don't want
> to go on with this forever in order to find that equipment).

I usually play this way.  A couple hints.  This is pretty spoily so be
forwarned.

1. Wield something useless like a  food ration.  This way if you bump
into something you probably won't kill it.

2. You've probably figured out keeping your pet close.  Try a leash, or
a whistle to call him away from floating eyes or red molds, or other
things that might get him in trouble.  Once you get a magic whistle
you're in easy.

3. Displacing your pet towards danger is a key technique, as is
stealing from shops with your pet.  Sell as much as possible,
especially spellbooks, minor rings, etc. to collect gold.  Don't worry,
you will get it all back.

4. Note where the vault entrances are.

5. The mines are full of tools and you should find something useful if
you can get a light source.  I usually play the first 5 or 6 dungeon
levels as pascifict and letting my pet do the work.  Collect gold, find
a lamp,  then try the mines.  Once I have about 1200+ gold and a light
source then I head for the mines.  If I have no light source I go to
the mines anyway.  Just be careful.   In the mines, you're specifically
looking for a lamp (if you don't have one yet), a leash, magic or tin
whistle, gold, pickaxe, and a polymorph trap.  Once you have a pickaxe,
go back up and loot the vaults.  I will let you guess what to do with
the poly trap.  Once you figure out what to do with it, getting your
gold back and looting all the shops is very easy.

